From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:37:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 137/151] Find: extended mode and capture groups in the replace
 text

Extended mode (Notepad++ "Extended"), a find option shown only without
regex, reads \n, \r, \t, \0, \\, \xNN and \uNNNN in the find and
replace text. Any other backslash, an incomplete \x or \u and a
surrogate are kept as typed. A find text with a line break after
unescaping is searched in the joined lines, where \n matches any line
ending unless the text also names \r.

In regex mode the replace text names capture groups: $1, ${name}, $0
and \0 to \9 as in Notepad++ (\10 is group 1 and a 0; ${1}0 too), with
$$ for a literal $ and the extended escapes. Normal and extended mode
keep $ literal. Replace, Replace all and the joined paths all expand
groups, and a line break in the replacement takes the file's ending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

